  "notes": "ばね refers to a mechanical spring or springiness. Can also be written as バネ or {発条|ばね}.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ばねが{効|き}く: to have good springs, to be springy\n- ばねが{壊|こわ}れる: the spring breaks\n- {足|あし}のばね: leg spring (jumping ability)\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- コイルばね: coil spring\n- {板|いた}ばね: leaf spring\n- ばね{仕掛|じか}け: spring-loaded\n\nFIGURATIVE:\nばね is often used figuratively to describe resilience or the ability to bounce back from adversity.",
